augmentationMap -- map from a free resolution to a module regarded as a complex
*******************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        augmentationMap C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, constructed via *note freeResolution:
        freeResolution,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, a quasi-isomorphism whose source
        is $C$ and whose target is the module resolved by $C$

Description
===========

Given a complex $C$, this method produces the natural quasi-isomorphism from a
complex $F$ all of whose terms are free modules to the complex $C$. The
algorithm used minimizes the ranks of the free modules in $F$.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                         |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^2, a*b, b*c)                   |
|                                                |
|             2                                  |
|o2 = ideal (a , a*b, b*c)                       |
|                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution I                       |
|                                                |
|      1      3      2                           |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                            |
|                                                |
|     0      1      2                            |
|                                                |
|o3 : Complex                                    |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = augmentationMap C                      |
|                                                |
|                                           1    |
|o4 = 0 : cokernel | a2 ab bc | <--------- R  : 0|
|                                  | 1 |         |
|                                                |
|o4 : ComplexMap                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : assert isWellDefined f                     |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert isComplexMorphism f                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert isQuasiIsomorphism f                |
+------------------------------------------------+
+------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : g = resolutionMap complex comodule I       |
|                                                |
|                                           1    |
|o8 = 0 : cokernel | a2 ab bc | <--------- R  : 0|
|                                  | 1 |         |
|                                                |
|o8 : ComplexMap                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(f == g)                             |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note resolutionMap(Complex): resolutionMap, -- map from a free resolution
    to the given complex
  * *note freeResolution(Module): freeResolution, -- compute a free resolution
    of a module or ideal
  * *note isQuasiIsomorphism(ComplexMap): isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp,
    -- whether a map of complexes is a quasi-isomorphism

Ways to use augmentationMap:
============================

  * "augmentationMap(Complex)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note augmentationMap: augmentationMap, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

