Basic invariants and properties -- information about accessing basic features
*****************************************************************************

Predicates for complexes and complex maps
=========================================

  * *note isWellDefined(Complex): isWellDefined_lpComplex_rp, -- whether a
    complex is well-defined
  * *note isExact(Complex): isExact_lpComplex_cmNumber_cmNumber_rp, -- whether
    a complex is exact
  * *note isHomogeneous(Complex): isHomogeneous_lpComplex_rp, -- whether a
    complex is homogeneous
  * *note isFree(Complex): isFree_lpComplex_rp, -- whether a complex consists
    of free modules
  * *note isShortExactSequence(Complex): isShortExactSequence_lpComplex_rp, --
    whether a chain complex is a short exact sequence
  * *note isWellDefined(ComplexMap): isWellDefined_lpComplexMap_rp, -- whether
    a map of chain complexes is well-defined
  * *note isCommutative(ComplexMap): isCommutative_lpComplexMap_rp, -- whether
    a complex map commutes with the differentials
  * *note isComplexMorphism(ComplexMap): isComplexMorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a complex map is a morphism of complexes
  * *note isQuasiIsomorphism(ComplexMap): isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp,
    -- whether a map of complexes is a quasi-isomorphism
  * *note isShortExactSequence(ComplexMap,ComplexMap):
    isShortExactSequence_lpComplexMap_cmComplexMap_rp, -- whether a pair of
    complex maps forms a short exact sequence
  * *note isNullHomotopic(ComplexMap): isNullHomotopic_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a map of complexes is null-homotopic
  * *note isNullHomotopyOf(ComplexMap,ComplexMap):
    isNullHomotopyOf_lpComplexMap_cmComplexMap_rp, -- whether the first map of
    chain complexes is a null homotopy for the second

Other invariants for complexes
==============================

  * *note ring(Complex): ring_lpComplex_rp, -- access the ring of a complex or
    a complex map
  * *note concentration(Complex): concentration, -- indices on which a complex
    may be non-zero
  * *note max(Complex): concentration, -- indices on which a complex may be
