canonicalTruncation(ComplexMap,ZZ,ZZ) -- reducing the number of non-zero terms of a complex
*******************************************************************************************

  * Function: *note canonicalTruncation:
    canonicalTruncation_lpComplex_cmZZ_cmZZ_rp,
  * Usage: 
        canonicalTruncation(f, (lo, hi))
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, which commutes with the
        differentials
      * lo, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or -infinity or null (the
        latter two give no lower bound)
      * hi, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, or infinity or null (the
        latter two give no upper bound)
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 

Description
===========

Returns a new complex map (commuting with the differentials) which drops (sets
to zero) all modules outside the given range in the source, and modifies the
ends to preserve homology in the given range.  The degree of the map f is used
to determine the truncation of the target.

First, we define some non-trivial maps of chain complexes.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------+
