ComplexMap * ComplexMap -- composition of homomorphisms of complexes
********************************************************************

  * Operator: *note *: (Macaulay2Doc)_st,
  * Usage: 
        f = h * g
  * Inputs:
      * h, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, if a ring element or integer,
        then we multiply the ring element by the appropriate identity map
      * g, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, the composition of $g$
        followed by $h$

Description
===========

If $g_i : C_i \rightarrow D_{d+i}$, and $h_j : D_j \rightarrow E_{e+j}$, then
the composition corresponds to $f_i := h_{d+i} * g_i : C_i \rightarrow
E_{i+d+e}$.  In particular, the degree of the composition $f$ is the sum of the
degrees of $g$ and $h$.

