ComplexMap ++ ComplexMap -- direct sum of complex maps
******************************************************

  * Operator: *note ++: (Macaulay2Doc)++,
  * Usage: 
        h = f ++ g
        h = directSum(f,g,...)
        h = directSum(name1 => f, name2 => g, ...)
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
      * g, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, that is the direct sum of the
        input chain  complex maps

Description
===========

The direct sum of two complex maps is a a complex map from the direct sum of
the sources to the direct sum of the targets.

First, we define some non-trivial maps of chain complexes.

