ComplexMap ^ Array -- the composition with the canonical inclusion or projection map
************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ^: (Macaulay2Doc)^,
  * Usage: 
        i = f_[name]
        p = f^[name]
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
      * name, an *note array: (Macaulay2Doc)Array,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, i is the composition of f with
        the canonical inclusion and p is the composition of the canonical
        projection with f

Description
===========

The direct sum is an n-ary operator with projection and inclusion maps from
each component satisfying appropriate identities.

One can access these maps as follows.  First, we define some non-trivial maps
of chain complexes.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..d];                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C1 = (freeResolution coker matrix{{a,b,c}})[1]                          |
|                                                                             |
|      1      3      3      1                                                 |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|     -1     0      1      2                                                  |
|                                                                             |
