Concentration -- optional argument used to specify the concentration
********************************************************************

Description
===========

In this package, each complex $C$ has a concentration $(\ell, h)$ such that
$\ell \leq h$.  For all $i < \ell$ and all $i > h$, the term $C_i$ is zero.
When $\ell \leq i \leq h$, the module $C_i$ may or may not be zero.

Several methods use this optional argument to specify the concentration of
their outputs.

See also
========

  * *note concentration(Complex): concentration, -- indices on which a complex
    may be non-zero

Functions with optional argument named Concentration:
=====================================================

  * "connectingExtMap(...,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    connectingExtMap(Module,Matrix,Matrix):
    connectingExtMap_lpModule_cmMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- makes the connecting
    maps in Ext
  * "connectingMap(...,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    connectingMap(ComplexMap,ComplexMap):
    connectingMap_lpComplexMap_cmComplexMap_rp, -- construct the connecting
    homomorphism on homology
  * "connectingTorMap(...,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    connectingTorMap(Module,Matrix,Matrix):
    connectingTorMap_lpModule_cmMatrix_cmMatrix_rp, -- makes the connecting
    maps in Tor
  * "isQuasiIsomorphism(...,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    isQuasiIsomorphism(ComplexMap): isQuasiIsomorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a map of complexes is a quasi-isomorphism
  * "koszulComplex(List,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    koszulComplex(Matrix): koszulComplex_lpMatrix_rp, -- makes the Koszul
    complex
  * "koszulComplex(Matrix,Concentration=>...)" -- see *note
    koszulComplex(Matrix): koszulComplex_lpMatrix_rp, -- makes the Koszul
