The connecting homomorphism fits into a natural long exact sequence in Tor.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : F = freeResolution kk;                             |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : LES = longExactSequence(F ** g, F ** f);           |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : assert all(3, i -> dd^LES_(3*(i+1)) == delta_(i+1))|
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert(HH LES == 0)                                |
+---------------------------------------------------------+

As a second example, applying the functor $- \otimes_S \Bbbk$ to a short exact
sequence of modules

$\phantom{WWWW} 0 \leftarrow S/(I+J) \leftarrow S/I \oplus S/J  \leftarrow S/I
\cap J \leftarrow 0 $

gives rise to the long exact sequence of Tor modules having the form

$\phantom{WWWW} \dotsb \leftarrow \operatorname{Tor}_{i-1}(S/(I+J), \Bbbk)
\xleftarrow{\delta_{i}} \operatorname{Tor}_i(S/I \cap J, \Bbbk) \leftarrow
\operatorname{Tor}_i(S/I \oplus S/J, \Bbbk) \leftarrow
\operatorname{Tor}_i(S/(I+J), \Bbbk) \leftarrow \dotsb. $

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
