dual(ComplexMap) -- the dual of a map of complexes
**************************************************

  * Function: *note dual: (Macaulay2Doc)dual,
  * Usage: 
        h = dual f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * h, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 

Description
===========

The map $f : C \to D$ of chain complexes over the ring $S$ induces the map $h =
Hom(f, S^1) : Hom(D, S^1) \to Hom(C,S^1)$ defined by $\phi \mapsto \phi f$.

+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a..c]                                           |
|                                                                |
|o1 = S                                                          |
|                                                                |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = freeResolution coker vars S                            |
|                                                                |
|      1      3      3      1                                    |
|o2 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S                                     |
|                                                                |
|     0      1      2      3                                     |
|                                                                |
|o2 : Complex                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = (freeResolution coker matrix{{a^2,a*b,b^3}})[-1]       |
|                                                                |
|      1      3      2                                           |
|o3 = S  <-- S  <-- S                                            |
|                                                                |
|     1      2      3                                            |
|                                                                |
|o3 : Complex                                                    |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : f = randomComplexMap(D,C)                                  |
|                                                                |
|                   1                                            |
|o4 = 0 : 0 <----- S  : 0                                        |
|              0                                                 |
|                                                                |
|          1                                                3    |
|     1 : S  <-------------------------------------------- S  : 1|
|               | 24a-36b-30c -29a+19b+19c -10a-29b-8c |         |
|                                                                |
|          3                           3                         |
|     2 : S  <----------------------- S  : 2                     |
|               {2} | -22 -24 -16 |                              |
|               {2} | -29 -38 39  |                              |
|               {3} | 0   0   0   |                              |
|                                                                |
|          2                  1                                  |
|     3 : S  <-------------- S  : 3                              |
|               {3} | 21 |                                       |
|               {4} | 0  |                                       |
|                                                                |
|o4 : ComplexMap                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : h = dual f                                                 |
|                                                                |
|           1                     2                              |
|o5 = -3 : S  <----------------- S  : -3                         |
|                {-3} | 21 0 |                                   |
|                                                                |
|           3                          3                         |
|     -2 : S  <---------------------- S  : -2                    |
|                {-2} | -22 -29 0 |                              |
|                {-2} | -24 -38 0 |                              |
|                {-2} | -16 39  0 |                              |
|                                                                |
|           3                             1                      |
|     -1 : S  <------------------------- S  : -1                 |
|                {-1} | 24a-36b-30c  |                           |
|                {-1} | -29a+19b+19c |                           |
|                {-1} | -10a-29b-8c  |                           |
|                                                                |
|o5 : ComplexMap                                                 |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : assert isWellDefined h                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : assert(h == Hom(f, S^1))                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert(source h == Hom(D,S^1))                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(target h == Hom(C,S^1))                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------------+

This routine is functorial.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : D' = (freeResolution coker matrix{{a^2,a*b,c^3}})[-1]|
|                                                           |
|       1      3      3      1                              |
|o10 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S                               |
|                                                           |
|      1      2      3      4                               |
|                                                           |
|o10 : Complex                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : f' = randomComplexMap(D', D)                         |
|                                                           |
|           1              1                                |
|o11 = 1 : S  <---------- S  : 1                            |
|                | 34 |                                     |
|                                                           |
|           3                                    3          |
|      2 : S  <-------------------------------- S  : 2      |
|                {2} | 19  -39 -13a-43b-15c |               |
|                {2} | -47 -18 -28a-47b+38c |               |
|                {3} | 0   0   2            |               |
|                                                           |
|           3                              2                |
|      3 : S  <-------------------------- S  : 3            |
|                {3} | 16 22a+45b-34c |                     |
|                {5} | 0  0           |                     |
|                {5} | 0  0           |                     |
|                                                           |
|o11 : ComplexMap                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : dual(f' * f) == dual f * dual f'                     |
|                                                           |
|o12 = true                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

For backwards compatibility, one can also use transpose.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : h' = transpose f                          |
|                                                |
|            1                     2             |
|o13 = -3 : S  <----------------- S  : -3        |
|                 {-3} | 21 0 |                  |
|                                                |
|            3                          3        |
|      -2 : S  <---------------------- S  : -2   |
|                 {-2} | -22 -29 0 |             |
|                 {-2} | -24 -38 0 |             |
|                 {-2} | -16 39  0 |             |
|                                                |
|            3                             1     |
|      -1 : S  <------------------------- S  : -1|
|                 {-1} | 24a-36b-30c  |          |
|                 {-1} | -29a+19b+19c |          |
|                 {-1} | -10a-29b-8c  |          |
|                                                |
|o13 : ComplexMap                                |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert(h == h')                           |
+------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Hom(ComplexMap,ComplexMap): Hom_lpComplexMap_cmComplexMap_rp, -- the
    map of complexes between Hom complexes
  * *note randomComplexMap(Complex,Complex):
    randomComplexMap_lpComplex_cmComplex_rp, -- a random map of chain complexes
  * *note dual(Matrix): (Macaulay2Doc)dual_lpMatrix_rp, -- dual of a map
  * *note transpose(Matrix): (Macaulay2Doc)transpose, -- transpose a matrix or
    table

Ways to use this method:
========================

