freeResolution -- compute a free resolution of a module or ideal
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        freeResolution M
        freeResolution I
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, in the ring $R$, treated as
        the quotient module $R^1/I$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note LengthLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, this is used to limit
        somehow the computation where resolutions might be too long or infinite
      * *note DegreeLimit: Options for free resolutions, => a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value infinity, or an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an option that specifies that the computation stops
        at the given (slanted) degree
      * *note HardDegreeLimit: Options for free resolutions, => a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {}, unused
      * *note PairLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, or *note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,, an internal option which specifies that the
        computation should stop after a certain number of s-pairs have computed
      * *note SortStrategy: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, an internal option that specifies
        the strategy to be used for sorting S-pairs
      * *note StopBeforeComputation: Options for free resolutions, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, whether to
        start the computation. This can be useful when you want to obtain the
        partially computed resolution contained in an interrupted computation.
      * *note Strategy: Strategies for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, one of the integers 0,1,2,3, one
        of the symbols Engine, Homogenization, Syzygies, Nonminimal, OverField,
        OverZZ, or null
      * *note SyzygyLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, or *note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,, an internal option which specifies that the
        computation should stop after a certain number of syzygies have
        computed
      * *note ParallelizeByDegree: Options for free resolutions, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, Use
        additional parallelism to compute different (homological degree,
        internal degree) pairs in parallel when possible. To control
        parallelism, see "parallelism in engine computations"
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: Complex,, a free resolution of the module $M$ or of
        the quotient module $R^1/I$

Description
===========

A free resolution of a module $M$ is a complex

$\phantom{WWWW} F_0 \leftarrow F_1 \leftarrow F_2 \leftarrow \dotsb $

of free modules, whose homology is concentrated in homological degree zero and
is isomorphic to the module $M$.  Equivalently, the augmented complex

$\phantom{WWWW} 0 \leftarrow M \leftarrow F_0 \leftarrow F_1 \leftarrow F_2
\leftarrow \dotsb $

is exact.

This function lies at the heart of many computations in commutative algebra and
algebraic geometry.  As a consequence, this is one of the most used functions
in Macaulay2.

As a first example, we construct the free resolution of the twisted cubic
curve, and extract its basic numerical invariants via *note length(Complex):
length_lpComplex_rp, and *note betti(Complex): betti_lpComplex_rp,.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                           |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(c^2-b*d, b*c-a*d, b^2-a*c)    |
|                                             |
|             2                    2          |
|o2 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d, b  - a*c)   |
|                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i3 : M = R^1/I                               |
|                                             |
|o3 = cokernel | c2-bd bc-ad b2-ac |          |
|                                             |
|                            1                |
|o3 : R-module, quotient of R                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = freeResolution M                    |
|                                             |
|      1      3      2                        |
|o4 = R  <-- R  <-- R                         |
|                                             |
|     0      1      2                         |
|                                             |
|o4 : Complex                                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i5 : length C                                |
|                                             |
|o5 = 2                                       |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i6 : betti C                                 |
|                                             |
|            0 1 2                            |
|o6 = total: 1 3 2                            |
|         0: 1 . .                            |
|         1: . 3 2                            |
|                                             |
|o6 : BettiTally                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i7 : dd^C                                    |
|                                             |
|          1                             3    |
|o7 = 0 : R  <------------------------- R  : 1|
|               | b2-ac bc-ad c2-bd |         |
|                                             |
|          3                     2            |
|     1 : R  <----------------- R  : 2        |
|               {2} | -c d  |                 |
|               {2} | b  -c |                 |
|               {2} | -a b  |                 |
|                                             |
|o7 : ComplexMap                              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert isWellDefined C                  |
+---------------------------------------------+

We verify in two ways that $C$ is a free resolution of $M$.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert(prune HH C == complex M)                      |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(length HH C == 0)                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i11 : f = augmentationMap C                               |
|                                                          |
|                                                     1    |
|o11 = 0 : cokernel | c2-bd bc-ad b2-ac | <--------- R  : 0|
|                                            | 1 |         |
|                                                          |
|o11 : ComplexMap                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : assert isWellDefined f                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : assert(source f === C)                              |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : assert(target f == complex M)                       |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : aC = cone f                                         |
|                                                          |
|             1      3      2                              |
|o15 = M <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                               |
|                                                          |
|      0     1      2      3                               |
|                                                          |
|o15 : Complex                                             |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : assert(HH aC == 0)                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

Giving an ideal as the input produces a free resolution not of the module $I$,
but of the comodule $R^1/I$.

+------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : assert(freeResolution I == C)                   |
+------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : assert(resolution complex M == freeResolution M)|
+------------------------------------------------------+

We obtain the resolution of the module $I$, rather than the comodule $R^1/I$,
as follows.

+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i19 : C' = freeResolution module I                                 |
|                                                                   |
|       3      2                                                    |
|o19 = R  <-- R                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|      0      1                                                     |
|                                                                   |
|o19 : Complex                                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i20 : assert isWellDefined C'                                      |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i21 : assert(C' != C)                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i22 : assert(betti naiveTruncation(C, 1, infinity) == betti C'[-1])|
