Over a quotient ring, free resolutions are typically infinite. To specify a
finite part of the resolution, one needs to use the optional argument
LengthLimit.

+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i23 : S = ZZ/101[a,b];                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i24 : R = S/(a^3+b^3);                                   |
+---------------------------------------------------------+
|i25 : C = freeResolution (coker vars R, LengthLimit => 7)|
|                                                         |
|       1      2      2      2      2      2      2      2|
|o25 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R |
|                                                         |
|      0      1      2      3      4      5      6      7 |
|                                                         |
|o25 : Complex                                            |
