freeResolution(Matrix) -- compute the induced map between free resolutions
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note freeResolution: freeResolution,
  * Usage: 
        freeResolution f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, defining a map from an
        $R$-module $M$ to an $R$-module $N$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note LengthLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, this is used to limit
        somehow the computation where resolutions might be too long or infinite
      * *note DegreeLimit: Options for free resolutions, => a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value infinity, or an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an option that specifies that the computation stops
        at the given (slanted) degree
      * *note HardDegreeLimit: Options for free resolutions, => a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value {}, unused (TODO: used?)
      * *note PairLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, or *note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,, an internal option which specifies that the
        computation should stop after a certain number of s-pairs have computed
      * *note SortStrategy: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, an internal option that specifies
        the strategy to be used for sorting S-pairs
      * *note StopBeforeComputation: Options for free resolutions, => a *note
        Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, default value false, whether to
        start the computation. This can be useful when you want to obtain the
        partially computed resolution contained in an interrupted computation.
      * *note Strategy: Strategies for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value null, TODO: perhaps needs its own page
      * *note SyzygyLimit: Options for free resolutions, => an *note integer:
        (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value infinity, or *note infinity:
        (Macaulay2Doc)infinity,, an internal option which specifies that the
        computation should stop after a certain number of syzygies have
        computed
      * *note ParallelizeByDegree: Options for free resolutions, => ...,
        default value false, optional arguments for freeResolution
  * Outputs:
      * a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, an induced map of chain
        complexes from the free resolution of $M$ to the free resolution of $N$

Description
===========

A homomorphism $f \colon M \to N$ of $R$-modules induces a morphism of chain
complexes from any free resolution of $M$ to a free resolution of $N$.  This
method constructs this map of chain complexes.

+-------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                         |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(c^2-b*d, b*c-a*d, b^2-a*c)  |
|                                           |
|             2                    2        |
|o2 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d, b  - a*c) |
|                                           |
|o2 : Ideal of R                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = ideal(I_0, I_1)                   |
|                                           |
|             2                             |
|o3 = ideal (c  - b*d, b*c - a*d)           |
|                                           |
|o3 : Ideal of R                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i4 : M = R^1/J                             |
|                                           |
|o4 = cokernel | c2-bd bc-ad |              |
|                                           |
|                            1              |
|o4 : R-module, quotient of R               |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i5 : N = R^1/I                             |
|                                           |
|o5 = cokernel | c2-bd bc-ad b2-ac |        |
|                                           |
|                            1              |
|o5 : R-module, quotient of R               |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i6 : f = map(N, M, 1)                      |
|                                           |
|o6 = | 1 |                                 |
|                                           |
|o6 : Matrix N <-- M                        |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i7 : g = freeResolution f                  |
|                                           |
|          1             1                  |
|o7 = 0 : R  <--------- R  : 0              |
|               | 1 |                       |
|                                           |
|          3                   2            |
|     1 : R  <--------------- R  : 1        |
|               {2} | 0 0 |                 |
|               {2} | 1 0 |                 |
|               {2} | 0 1 |                 |
|                                           |
|          2                  1             |
|     2 : R  <-------------- R  : 2         |
|               {3} | -d |                  |
|               {3} | -c |                  |
|                                           |
|o7 : ComplexMap                            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert isWellDefined g                |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i9 : assert isComplexMorphism g            |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(source g === freeResolution M)|
+-------------------------------------------+
|i11 : assert(target g === freeResolution N)|
+-------------------------------------------+

Taking free resolutions is a functor, up to homotopy, from the category of
modules to the category of chain complexes. In the subsequent example, the
composition of the induced chain maps $g$ and $g'$ happens to be equal to the
induced map of the composition.

+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : K = ideal(I_0)                                       |
|                                                           |
|             2                                             |
|o12 = ideal(c  - b*d)                                      |
|                                                           |
|o12 : Ideal of R                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : L = R^1/K                                            |
|                                                           |
|o13 = cokernel | c2-bd |                                   |
|                                                           |
|                             1                             |
|o13 : R-module, quotient of R                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : f' = map(M, L, 1)                                    |
|                                                           |
|o14 = | 1 |                                                |
|                                                           |
|o14 : Matrix M <-- L                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : g' = freeResolution f'                               |
|                                                           |
|           1             1                                 |
|o15 = 0 : R  <--------- R  : 0                             |
|                | 1 |                                      |
|                                                           |
|           2                 1                             |
|      1 : R  <------------- R  : 1                         |
|                {2} | 0 |                                  |
|                {2} | 1 |                                  |
|                                                           |
|o15 : ComplexMap                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i16 : g'' = freeResolution(f * f')                         |
|                                                           |
|           1             1                                 |
|o16 = 0 : R  <--------- R  : 0                             |
|                | 1 |                                      |
|                                                           |
|           3                 1                             |
|      1 : R  <------------- R  : 1                         |
|                {2} | 0 |                                  |
|                {2} | 0 |                                  |
|                {2} | 1 |                                  |
|                                                           |
|o16 : ComplexMap                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i17 : assert(g'' === g * g')                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------+
|i18 : assert(freeResolution id_N === id_(freeResolution N))|
+-----------------------------------------------------------+

Over a quotient ring, free resolutions are often infinite. Use the optional
argument LengthLimit to obtain a truncation of the map between resolutions.

+---------------------------------------------+
|i19 : S = ZZ/101[a,b]                        |
|                                             |
|o19 = S                                      |
|                                             |
|o19 : PolynomialRing                         |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i20 : R = S/(a^3+b^3)                        |
|                                             |
|o20 = R                                      |
|                                             |
|o20 : QuotientRing                           |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i21 : f = map(R^1/(a,b), R^1/(a^2, b^2), 1)  |
|                                             |
|o21 = | 1 |                                  |
|                                             |
|o21 : Matrix                                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i22 : g = freeResolution(f, LengthLimit => 7)|
|                                             |
|           1             1                   |
|o22 = 0 : R  <--------- R  : 0               |
|                | 1 |                        |
|                                             |
|           2                   2             |
|      1 : R  <--------------- R  : 1         |
|                {1} | a 0 |                  |
|                {1} | 0 b |                  |
|                                             |
|           2                    2            |
|      2 : R  <---------------- R  : 2        |
|                {2} | 0 ab |                 |
|                {3} | 1 0  |                 |
|                                             |
|           2                   2             |
|      3 : R  <--------------- R  : 3         |
|                {4} | 0 b |                  |
|                {4} | a 0 |                  |
|                                             |
|           2                     2           |
|      4 : R  <----------------- R  : 4       |
|                {5} | 0 -ab |                |
|                {6} | 1 0   |                |
|                                             |
|           2                   2             |
|      5 : R  <--------------- R  : 5         |
|                {7} | 0 b |                  |
|                {7} | a 0 |                  |
|                                             |
|           2                     2           |
|      6 : R  <----------------- R  : 6       |
|                {8} | 0 -ab |                |
|                {9} | 1 0   |                |
|                                             |
|           2                    2            |
|      7 : R  <---------------- R  : 7        |
|                {10} | 0 b |                 |
|                {10} | a 0 |                 |
|                                             |
|o22 : ComplexMap                             |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i23 : assert isWellDefined g                 |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i24 : assert isComplexMorphism g             |
+---------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Making maps between chain complexes: Making maps between chain
    complexes, -- information about the basic constructors
  * *note freeResolution(Module): freeResolution, -- compute a free resolution
    of a module or ideal
  * *note isComplexMorphism(ComplexMap): isComplexMorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a complex map is a morphism of complexes

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note freeResolution(Matrix): freeResolution_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute the
    induced map between free resolutions
