HH_ZZ Complex -- homology or cohomology module of a complex
***********************************************************

  * Function: *note homology: (Macaulay2Doc)homology,
  * Usage: 
        HH_i C
        HH^i C
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the $i$-th homology or
        cohomology of the complex

Description
===========

The $i$-th homology of a complex $C$ is the quotient (ker dd^C_i/image
dd^C_(i+1)).

The first example is the complex associated to a triangulation of the real
projective plane, having 6 vertices, 15 edges, and 10 triangles.

