Hom(Complex,Complex) -- the complex of homomorphisms between two complexes
**************************************************************************

  * Function: *note Hom: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom,
  * Usage: 
        D = Hom(C1,C2)
  * Inputs:
      * C1, a *note complex: Complex,, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,,
        or a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,
      * C2, a *note complex: Complex,, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,,
        or a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,,
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note DegreeLimit: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
      * *note MinimalGenerators: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value true,
      * *note Strategy: (Macaulay2Doc)Hom, => ..., default value null, 
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note complex: Complex,, the complex of homomorphisms between C1
        and C2

Description
===========

The complex of homomorphisms is a complex $D$ whose $i$th component is the
direct sum of $\operatorname{Hom}(C1_j, C2_{j+i})$ over all $j$. The
differential on $\operatorname{Hom}(C1_j, C2_{j+i})$ is the differential
$\operatorname{Hom}(id_{C1}, dd^{C2}) + (-1)^j \operatorname{Hom}(dd^{C1},
id_{C2})$. $dd^{C1} \otimes id_{C2} + (-1)^j id_{C1} \otimes dd^{C2}$.

In particular, for this operation to be well-defined, both arguments must have
the same underlying ring.

