homomorphism(ZZ,Matrix,Complex) -- get the homomorphism from an element of Hom
******************************************************************************

  * Function: *note homomorphism: (Macaulay2Doc)homomorphism,
  * Usage: 
        g = homomorphism(i, f, E)
  * Inputs:
      * i, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * f, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a map of the form $f \colon
        R^1 \to E_i$
      * E, a *note complex: Complex,, having the form $E =
        \operatorname{Hom}(C, D)$ for some complexes $C$ and $D$
  * Outputs:
      * g, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, the corresponding map of
        chain complexes from $C$ to $D$ of degree $i$

Description
===========

An element of the complex $\operatorname{Hom}(C, D)$ corresponds to a map of
complexes from $C$ to $D$.  Given an element in the $i$-th term, this method
returns the corresponding map of complexes of degree $i$.

As a first example, consider two Koszul complexes $C$ and $D$. From a random
map $f \colon R^1 \to \operatorname{Hom}(C, D)$, we construct the corresponding
map of chain complexes $g \colon C \to D$.

