horseshoeResolution(Complex) -- make the horseshoe resolution
*************************************************************

  * Function: *note horseshoeResolution: horseshoeResolution_lpComplex_rp,
  * Usage: 
        (beta, alpha) = horseshoeResolution C
        (beta, alpha) = horseshoeResolution(g, f)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, (or a pair of maps) that is a short exact
        sequence of modules
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * LengthLimit => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value
        infinity, limit the lengths of the constructed free resolutions
  * Outputs:
      * a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, consisting of a pair of
        chain complex maps $\beta$ and $\alpha$

Description
===========

Given a short exact sequence of modules

$\phantom{WWWW} 0 \leftarrow N \xleftarrow{g} M \xleftarrow{f} L \leftarrow 0,
$

the horsehoe lemma produces simultaneous free resolutions of $N$, $M$ and $L$,
which form a short exact sequence of complexes. This method returns these two
chain complex maps.

We illustrate this method by constructing simultaneous free resolutions of
three monomial ideals.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^3, b^3, c^3)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|             3   3   3                                                       |
|o2 = ideal (a , b , c )                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : J = I + ideal(a*b*c)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|             3   3   3                                                       |
|o3 = ideal (a , b , c , a*b*c)                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = I : ideal(a*b*c)                                                    |
|                                                                             |
|             2   2   2                                                       |
|o4 = ideal (c , b , a )                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C = complex{                                                            |
|         map(comodule J, comodule I, 1),                                     |
|         map(comodule I, (comodule K) ** S^{-3}, {{a*b*c}})                  |
|         }                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = cokernel | a3 b3 c3 abc | <-- cokernel | a3 b3 c3 | <-- cokernel {3} |  |
