isCommutative(ComplexMap) -- whether a complex map commutes with the differentials
**********************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isCommutative: (Macaulay2Doc)isCommutative,
  * Usage: 
        isCommutative f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when $f$
        commutes with the differentials

Description
===========

For a complex map $f : C \to D$ of degree $d$, this method checks whether, for
all $i$, we have $dd^D_{i+d} * f_i = (-1)^d * (f_{i-1} * dd^C_i)$.

We first construct a random complex map which commutes with the differential.

