isWellDefined(ComplexMap) -- whether a map of chain complexes is well-defined
*****************************************************************************

  * Function: *note isWellDefined: (Macaulay2Doc)isWellDefined,
  * Usage: 
        isWellDefined f
  * Inputs:
      * f, a *note map of complexes: ComplexMap,, 
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, that is true when f
        determines a well defined complex map

Description
===========

A map of chain complexes $f : C \to D$ of degree $d$ is a sequence of maps $f_i
: C_i \to D_{d+i}$.  No relationship is required between these maps and the
differentials in the source and target.

This routine checks that $C$ and $D$ are well-defined chain complexes, and
that, for each $f_i$, the source and target equal $C_i$ and $D_{d+i}$,
respectively.  If the variable debugLevel is set to a value greater than zero,
then information about the nature of any failure is displayed.

Unlike the *note corresponding function for Complexes:
isWellDefined_lpComplex_rp,, the basic constructors for complex maps are all
but assured to be well defined. The only case that could cause a problem is if
one constructs the source or target complex, and those are not well defined.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a,b,c];                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = freeResolution coker matrix{{a^2-b^2,b^3-c^3,c^4}}                  |
|                                                                             |
|      1      3      3      1                                                 |
|o2 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2      3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : D = freeResolution coker vars R                                         |
|                                                                             |
|      1      3      3      1                                                 |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2      3                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : H = hashTable { 0 => map(D_0, C_0, 1),                                  |
|         1 => map(D_1, C_1, {{a, 0, 0}, {-b, b^2, 0}, {0, -c^2, c^3}}),      |
|         2 => map(D_2, C_2, {{a*b^2, 0, 0}, {-a*c^2, a*c^3, 0}, {b*c^2,      |
|         3 => map(D_3, C_3, {{a*b^2*c^3}})                                   |
|         }                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = HashTable{0 => | 1 |                 }                                  |
