Making chain complexes -- information about the basic constructors
******************************************************************

Basic constructors
==================

  * *note complex(HashTable): complex_lpHashTable_rp, -- make a chain complex
  * *note complex(List): complex_lpList_rp, -- make a chain complex
  * *note complex(Module): complex_lpModule_rp, -- make a chain complex of
    length zero
  * *note complex(Complex): complex_lpComplex_rp, -- make a complex by
    reindexing the terms of the complex
  * *note Complex Array: Complex Array, -- shift a complex or complex map
  * *note isWellDefined(Complex): isWellDefined_lpComplex_rp, -- whether a
    complex is well-defined

Important computations creating new complexes
=============================================

  * *note freeResolution(Module): freeResolution, -- compute a free resolution
    of a module or ideal
  * *note freeResolution(Complex): freeResolution_lpComplex_rp, -- minimal free
    resolution of a complex
  * *note HH Complex: HH Complex, -- homology of a complex

More advanced constructors
==========================

  * *note Complex ++ Complex: directSum_lpComplex_rp, -- direct sum of
    complexes
  * *note Complex ** Complex: Complex _st_st Complex, -- tensor product of
    complexes
  * *note Hom(Complex,Complex): Hom_lpComplex_cmComplex_rp, -- the complex of
    homomorphisms between two complexes
  * *note dual(Complex): dual_lpComplex_rp, -- make the dual of a complex
  * *note RingMap Complex: RingMap Complex, -- apply a ring map
  * *note RingMap ** Complex: RingMap _st_st Complex, -- tensor a complex along
    a ring map
  * *note koszulComplex(Matrix): koszulComplex_lpMatrix_rp, -- makes the Koszul
    complex
  * eagonNorthcottComplex(Matrix) (missing documentation)
  * *note naiveTruncation(Complex,ZZ,ZZ):
    naiveTruncation_lpComplex_cmZZ_cmZZ_rp, -- drops all terms of a complex
    outside a given interval
  * *note canonicalTruncation(Complex,ZZ,ZZ):
    canonicalTruncation_lpComplex_cmZZ_cmZZ_rp, -- reducing the number of
    non-zero terms of a complex
  * *note minimalPresentation(Complex): minimalPresentation_lpComplex_rp, --
    minimal presentation of all terms in a complex
  * *note minimize(Complex): minimize_lpComplex_rp, -- a quasi-isomorphic
    complex whose terms have minimal rank
  * *note gradedModule(Complex): gradedModule_lpComplex_rp, -- a new complex in
    which the differential is zero
  * *note part(List,Complex): part_lpList_cmComplex_rp, -- extract a graded
    component of a complex
  * *note truncate(List,Complex): truncate_lpList_cmComplex_rp, -- truncation
    of a complex at a specified degree or set of degrees
  * *note yonedaExtension(Matrix): yonedaExtension_lpMatrix_rp, -- creates a
    chain complex representing an extension of modules

Extracting complexes from complex maps
======================================

  * *note source(ComplexMap): source_lpComplexMap_rp, -- get the source of a
    map of chain complexes
  * *note target(ComplexMap): target_lpComplexMap_rp, -- get the target of a
    map of chain complexes
  * *note kernel(ComplexMap): kernel_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the kernel of a
    map of complexes
  * *note cokernel(ComplexMap): cokernel_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the cokernel
    of a map of complexes
  * *note image(ComplexMap): image_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the image of a map
    of complexes
  * *note coimage(ComplexMap): coimage_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the coimage of
    a map of complexes
  * *note cone(ComplexMap): cone_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the mapping cone of a
    morphism of chain complexes
  * *note cylinder(ComplexMap): cylinder, -- make the mapping cylinder of a
    morphism of chain complexes

