Making maps between chain complexes -- information about the basic constructors
*******************************************************************************

Basic constructors
==================

  * *note map(Complex,Complex,HashTable):
    map_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmHashTable_rp, -- make a map of chain complexes
  * *note map(Complex,Complex,ZZ): map_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmZZ_rp, -- make the
    zero map or identity between chain complexes
  * *note map(Complex,Complex,Function): map_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmFunction_rp,
    -- make a map of chain complexes
  * *note map(Complex,Complex,List): map_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmList_rp, -- make
    a map of chain complexes
  * *note map(Complex,Complex,ComplexMap):
    map_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmComplexMap_rp, -- make a new map of chain
    complexes from an existing one
  * *note id _ Complex: id _us Complex, -- the identity map of a chain complex
  * *note differential of a chain complex: differential of a chain complex, --
    get the maps between the terms in a complex
  * *note ComplexMap Array: Complex Array, -- shift a complex or complex map
  * *note isWellDefined(ComplexMap): isWellDefined_lpComplexMap_rp, -- whether
    a map of chain complexes is well-defined

Important computations creating new complex maps
================================================

  * *note resolutionMap(Complex): resolutionMap, -- map from a free resolution
    to the given complex
  * *note HH ComplexMap: HH ComplexMap, -- induced map on homology or
    cohomology
  * *note augmentationMap(Complex): augmentationMap, -- map from a free
    resolution to a module regarded as a complex
  * *note Complex ** Matrix: Complex _st_st Matrix, -- create the tensor
    product of a complex and a map of modules
  * *note freeResolution(Matrix): freeResolution_lpMatrix_rp, -- compute the
    induced map between free resolutions
  * *note extend(Complex,Complex,Matrix):
    extend_lpComplex_cmComplex_cmMatrix_cmSequence_rp, -- extend a map of
    modules to a map of chain complexes
  * *note nullHomotopy(ComplexMap): nullHomotopy_lpComplexMap_rp, -- a map
    which is a candidate for being a null homotopy

Canonical maps between complexes
================================

Some complexes come with canonical maps. To access the complex map, one uses
*note canonicalMap(Complex,Complex): canonicalMap,. The following operations
have associated canonical maps.

  * *note kernel(ComplexMap): kernel_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the kernel of a
    map of complexes
  * *note cokernel(ComplexMap): cokernel_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the cokernel
    of a map of complexes
  * *note image(ComplexMap): image_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the image of a map
    of complexes
  * *note coimage(ComplexMap): coimage_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the coimage of
    a map of complexes
  * *note cone(ComplexMap): cone_lpComplexMap_rp, -- make the mapping cone of a
    morphism of chain complexes
  * *note cylinder(ComplexMap): cylinder, -- make the mapping cylinder of a
    morphism of chain complexes
  * *note inducedMap(Complex,Complex): inducedMap_lpComplex_cmComplex_rp, --
    make the map of complexes induced at each term by the identity map

Random maps of chain complexes
==============================

The method *note randomComplexMap(Complex,Complex):
randomComplexMap_lpComplex_cmComplex_rp, allows one to construct random complex
maps, random morphisms between complexes, and random null homotopies between
complexes.

  * *note isCommutative(ComplexMap): isCommutative_lpComplexMap_rp, -- whether
    a complex map commutes with the differentials
  * *note isComplexMorphism(ComplexMap): isComplexMorphism_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a complex map is a morphism of complexes
  * *note isNullHomotopic(ComplexMap): isNullHomotopic_lpComplexMap_rp, --
    whether a map of complexes is null-homotopic

Elementary operations on complex maps
=====================================

  * *note arithmetic with complex maps: arithmetic with complex maps, --
    perform arithmetic operations on complex maps
  * *note ComplexMap + ComplexMap: arithmetic with complex maps, -- perform
    arithmetic operations on complex maps
  * *note ComplexMap | ComplexMap: ComplexMap | ComplexMap, -- join or
    concatenate maps horizontally
  * *note ComplexMap || ComplexMap: ComplexMap || ComplexMap, -- join or
    concatenate maps vertically
  * *note ComplexMap ++ ComplexMap: ComplexMap ++ ComplexMap, -- direct sum of
    complex maps
  * *note ComplexMap ** ComplexMap: ComplexMap _st_st ComplexMap, -- the map of
    complexes between tensor complexes
  * *note Hom(ComplexMap,ComplexMap): Hom_lpComplexMap_cmComplexMap_rp, -- the
    map of complexes between Hom complexes
  * *note dual(ComplexMap): dual_lpComplexMap_rp, -- the dual of a map of
    complexes
  * *note ComplexMap _ Array: ComplexMap ^ Array, -- the composition with the
    canonical inclusion or projection map
  * *note ComplexMap ^ Array: ComplexMap ^ Array, -- the composition with the
    canonical inclusion or projection map
  * *note naiveTruncation(ComplexMap,Sequence):
    naiveTruncation_lpComplexMap_cmZZ_cmZZ_rp, -- drops all terms in the source
