pruneDiff -- Prunes a single differential in a chain complex or list of mutable matrices
****************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        D = pruneDiff(C, n)
        D = pruneDiff(C, n, M)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, or a list of mutable matrices defining
        the differentials of a complex
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the index of the differential
        in C
      * M, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, if provided, will initialize the
        map back to the original complex
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note PruningMap: PruningMap, => ..., default value true, Whether to
        compute a morphism of complexes
      * *note UnitTest: UnitTest, => ..., default value isUnit, Limit which
        units are to be pruned
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note complex: Complex,, or the list of modified mutable matrices
      * M, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, unless PruningMap is false, will
        contain the map back to the original complex

Description
===========

Completely prunes the n-th differential of the chain complex C by removing unit
elements.

Computing the syzygy over a local ring using liftUp and pruneDiff:

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : needsPackage "LocalRings";                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R = ZZ/32003[vars(0..5)];                               |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = ideal"abc-def,ab2-cd2-c,-b3+acd";                   |
|                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : C = freeResolution I;                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = ideal gens R;                                       |
|                                                             |
|o5 : Ideal of R                                              |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : RM = localRing(R, M);                                   |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : F = C.dd_2;                                             |
|                                                             |
|             4      6                                        |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R                                         |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : FM = F ** RM                                            |
|                                                             |
|o8 = {3} | 0    0    -b3+acd   -abc+def  0       a2c2-b2ef  ||
|     {3} | cef  ac2  ab2-cd2-c 0         abc-def -ac2d+abef ||
|     {3} | -ac2 -b2c 0         ab2-cd2-c -b3+acd -a2bc+b2cd ||
|     {5} | b    d    0         0         0       1          ||
|                                                             |
|              4       6                                      |
|o8 : Matrix RM  <-- RM                                       |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

This is the process for finding the syzygy of FM:

+-------------------------------------------+
|i9 : f = liftUp FM;                        |
|                                           |
|             4      6                      |
|o9 : Matrix R  <-- R                       |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i10 : g = syz f;                           |
|                                           |
|              6      5                     |
|o10 : Matrix R  <-- R                      |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i11 : h = syz g;                           |
|                                           |
|              5      2                     |
|o11 : Matrix R  <-- R                      |
+-------------------------------------------+
|i12 : C = {g ** RM, h ** RM}/mutableMatrix;|
+-------------------------------------------+

Now we prune the map h, which is the first map from the right:

+----------------------------------------------+
|i13 : C = pruneDiff(C, 1, PruningMap => false)|
|                                              |
|o13 = {| -d d2+1 0   |, 0}                    |
|       | b  -bd  -1  |                        |
|       | 0  ef   -ac |                        |
|       | 0  -ac  b2  |                        |
|       | -c 0    ab  |                        |
|       | 0  -b   d   |                        |
|                                              |
|o13 : List                                    |
+----------------------------------------------+
|i14 : g' = C#0;                               |
+----------------------------------------------+

Scale each row with the common denominator of the corresponding column in FM:

+---------------------------------------------+
|i15 : N = transpose entries FM;              |
+---------------------------------------------+
|i16 : for i from 0 to numcols FM - 1 do      |
|        rowMult(g', i, N_i/denominator//lcm);|
+---------------------------------------------+

The syzygy of FM is:

+--------------------------------------+
|i17 : GM = map(source FM, , matrix g')|
|                                      |
|o17 = {6} | -d d2+1 0   |             |
|      {6} | b  -bd  -1  |             |
|      {6} | 0  ef   -ac |             |
|      {6} | 0  -ac  b2  |             |
|      {6} | -c 0    ab  |             |
|      {7} | 0  -b   d   |             |
|                                      |
|               6       3              |
|o17 : Matrix RM  <-- RM               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i18 : kernel FM == image GM           |
|                                      |
|o18 = true                            |
+--------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This method does not use the algorithms in the engine, hence it might be slow.

See also
========

  * *note pruneUnit: pruneUnit, -- Prunes a unit of a differential in a list of
    mutable matrices
  * *note pruneComplex: pruneComplex, -- Prunes a chain complex or list of
    mutable matrices

Ways to use pruneDiff:
======================

  * "pruneDiff(Complex,ZZ)"
  * "pruneDiff(Complex,ZZ,List)"
  * "pruneDiff(List,ZZ)"
  * "pruneDiff(List,ZZ,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note pruneDiff: pruneDiff, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

