pruneUnit -- Prunes a unit of a differential in a list of mutable matrices
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        D = pruneUnit(C, n, u, M)
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of mutable matrices
        defining the differentials of a complex
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the index of the differential
        in C
      * u, a *note sequence: (Macaulay2Doc)Sequence,, the coordinates of the
        unit in the differential
      * M, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, if provided, will initialize the
        list of map back to the original complex
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note PruningMap: PruningMap, => ..., default value true, Whether to
        compute a morphism of complexes
      * *note UnitTest: UnitTest, => ..., default value isUnit, Limit which
        units are to be pruned
  * Outputs:
      * D, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of modified mutable
        matrices

Description
===========

Prune the unit in location {u} of the {n}-th differential in chain complex {C}.
Moves the unit to the end, clears row and column, while keeping the neighboring
differentials compatible.

Caveat
======

Currently only works with 1x1 units.

See also
========

  * *note pruningMap: (Macaulay2Doc)pruningMap,
  * *note pruneDiff: pruneDiff, -- Prunes a single differential in a chain
    complex or list of mutable matrices

Ways to use pruneUnit:
======================

  * "pruneUnit(List,ZZ,Sequence,List)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note pruneUnit: pruneUnit, is a *note method function with options:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunctionWithOptions,.

