regularity(Complex) -- compute the Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity
*****************************************************************

  * Function: *note regularity: (Macaulay2Doc)regularity,
  * Usage: 
        regularity C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note Weights: (Macaulay2Doc)regularity, => a *note list:
        (Macaulay2Doc)List,, default value null, for more information, see
        *note regularity(...,Weights=>...): (Macaulay2Doc)regularity,
  * Outputs:
      * an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 

Description
===========

Given a free complex $C$ over a standard graded polynomial ring, the regularity
$r$ of $C$ is the smallest integer such that each basis element of $C_i$ has
degree at most $i + r$.

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/101[a..d];                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(b^2-a*c, b*c-a*d, c^2-b*d)      |
|                                               |
|             2                    2            |
|o2 = ideal (b  - a*c, b*c - a*d, c  - b*d)     |
|                                               |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : C = freeResolution(R^1/I)                 |
|                                               |
|      1      3      2                          |
|o3 = R  <-- R  <-- R                           |
|                                               |
|     0      1      2                           |
|                                               |
|o3 : Complex                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i4 : betti C                                   |
|                                               |
|            0 1 2                              |
|o4 = total: 1 3 2                              |
|         0: 1 . .                              |
|         1: . 3 2                              |
|                                               |
|o4 : BettiTally                                |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i5 : regularity C                              |
|                                               |
|o5 = 1                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i6 : regularity I                              |
|                                               |
|o6 = 2                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i7 : regularity (R^1/I)                        |
|                                               |
|o7 = 1                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i8 : assert(regularity C === regularity(R^1/I))|
+-----------------------------------------------+

The regularity is the label of the last row of the Betti table of $C$.

+----------------------+
|i9 : betti C          |
|                      |
|            0 1 2     |
|o9 = total: 1 3 2     |
|         0: 1 . .     |
|         1: . 3 2     |
|                      |
|o9 : BettiTally       |
+----------------------+
|i10 : betti(C[3])     |
|                      |
|             -3 -2 -1 |
|o10 = total:  1  3  2 |
|          3:  1  .  . |
|          4:  .  3  2 |
|                      |
|o10 : BettiTally      |
+----------------------+
|i11 : regularity(C[3])|
|                      |
|o11 = 4               |
+----------------------+

Here is a slightly more complicated example.

+-------------------------------------------------+
|i12 : J = ideal(a^3, b^3, c^3, d^3, (a+b+c+d)^3);|
|                                                 |
|o12 : Ideal of R                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i13 : FJ = freeResolution J                      |
|                                                 |
|       1      5      17      20      7           |
|o13 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R   <-- R            |
|                                                 |
|      0      1      2       3       4            |
|                                                 |
|o13 : Complex                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i14 : betti FJ                                   |
|                                                 |
|             0 1  2  3 4                         |
|o14 = total: 1 5 17 20 7                         |
|          0: 1 .  .  . .                         |
|          1: . .  .  . .                         |
|          2: . 5  .  . .                         |
|          3: . .  .  . .                         |
|          4: . . 16 10 1                         |
|          5: . .  1 10 6                         |
|                                                 |
|o14 : BettiTally                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------+
|i15 : regularity FJ                              |
|                                                 |
|o15 = 5                                          |
+-------------------------------------------------+

Although Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity is defined in more general settings
(e.g. toric varieties with multi-degrees) this method does not currently handle
these extensions.  Similarly, Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity can be defined for
non-free complexes, but this method doesn't handle that case either.

See also
========

  * *note Basic invariants and properties: Basic invariants and properties, --
    information about accessing basic features
  * *note regularity: (Macaulay2Doc)regularity, -- compute the
    Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity
  * *note betti: (Macaulay2Doc)betti, -- display or modify a Betti diagram
  * *note freeResolution: freeResolution, -- compute a free resolution of a
    module or ideal

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note regularity(Complex): regularity_lpComplex_rp, -- compute the
    Castelnuovo-Mumford regularity
