ring(Complex) -- access the ring of a complex or a complex map
**************************************************************

  * Function: *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)ring,
  * Usage: 
        ring C
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, or a *note ComplexMap: ComplexMap,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, 

Description
===========

Every complex or complex map has a base ring.  This function access that
information.

+------------------------------------+
|i1 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d];           |
+------------------------------------+
|i2 : C = freeResolution coker vars S|
|                                    |
|      1      4      6      4      1 |
|o2 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S  |
|                                    |
|     0      1      2      3      4  |
|                                    |
|o2 : Complex                        |
+------------------------------------+
|i3 : ring C                         |
|                                    |
|o3 = S                              |
|                                    |
|o3 : PolynomialRing                 |
+------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(ring C === S)           |
+------------------------------------+
|i5 : ring id_C                      |
|                                    |
