RingMap ** Complex -- tensor a complex along a ring map
*******************************************************

  * Operator: *note **: (Macaulay2Doc)_st_st,
  * Usage: 
        phi ** C
        tensor(phi, C)
        S ** C
        C ** S
  * Inputs:
      * phi, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, whose source is a ring
        $R$ and whose target is a ring $S$
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, over the ring $R$
  * Outputs:
      * a *note complex: Complex,, over the ring $S$

Description
===========

These methods implement the base change of rings.  As input, one can either
give a ring map $\phi$, or the ring $S$ (when there is a canonical map from $R$
to $S$).

We illustrate the tensor product of a complex along a ring map.

+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z];                                                        |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = QQ[s,t];                                                          |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : phi = map(S, R, {s, s+t, t})                                          |
|                                                                           |
|o3 = map (S, R, {s, s + t, t})                                             |
|                                                                           |
|o3 : RingMap S <-- R                                                       |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal(x^3, x^2*y, x*y^4, y*z^5)                                   |
|                                                                           |
|             3   2      4     5                                            |
|o4 = ideal (x , x y, x*y , y*z )                                           |
|                                                                           |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                            |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C = freeResolution I                                                  |
|                                                                           |
|      1      4      4      1                                               |
|o5 = R  <-- R  <-- R  <-- R                                                |
|                                                                           |
|     0      1      2      3                                                |
|                                                                           |
|o5 : Complex                                                               |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : D = phi ** C                                                          |
|                                                                           |
|      1      4      4      1                                               |
|o6 = S  <-- S  <-- S  <-- S                                                |
|                                                                           |
|     0      1      2      3                                                |
|                                                                           |
|o6 : Complex                                                               |
