Strategies for free resolutions -- overview of the different algorithms for computing free resolutions
******************************************************************************************************

There are several distinct algorithms for computing free resolutions in
Macaulay2.  They make different assumptions about the module or underlying
ring.

  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => OverField): Strategy for free
    resolutions over a field, -- algorithm for computing free resolutions over
    a field
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => OverZZ): Strategy for free
    resolutions over the integers, -- algorithm for computing free resolutions
    of ZZ-modules
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => Engine):
    freeResolution_lp_pd_pd_pd_cm Strategy => Engine_rp, -- algorithm for
    computing a free resolution
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => 1): Default strategy for free
    resolutions of homogeneous modules, -- algorithm for computing free
    resolutions exploiting the Schreyer frame
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => 3): Strategy for free resolutions of
    homogeneous modules aided by Hilbert functions, -- algorithm for computing
    free resolutions step by step aided by Hilbert functions
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => 2): Strategy for free resolutions of
    homogeneous modules via successive syzygies, -- algorithm for computing
    free resolutions step by step
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => 0): Strategy for free resolutions via
    Schreyer-Lascala, -- algorithm for computing free resolutions exploiting
    the Schreyer frame
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => Homogenization): Strategy for free
    resolutions via homogenization, -- algorithm for computing free resolutions
    by first homogenizing
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => Syzygies): Strategy for free
    resolutions via syzygies, -- algorithm for computing free resolutions step
    by step using syzygies
  * *note freeResolution(..., Strategy => Nonminimal): Strategy for nonminimal
    free resolutions, -- algorithm for computing nonminimal free resolutions

One can always access the full list of possible strategies in Macaulay2 as
follows.

+------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : hooks freeResolution                                         |
|                                                                  |
|o1 = {0 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => NonminimalWithGB)}|
|     {1 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => Nonminimal)      }|
|     {2 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => Syzygies)        }|
|     {3 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => Homogenization)  }|
|     {4 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => 0)               }|
|     {5 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => 2)               }|
|     {6 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => 3)               }|
|     {7 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => 1)               }|
|     {8 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => Engine)          }|
|     {9 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => OverZZ)          }|
|     {10 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => OverField)      }|
|     {11 => (freeResolution, Module, Strategy => Local)          }|
|                                                                  |
|o1 : NumberedVerticalList                                         |
+------------------------------------------------------------------+

