This strategy works degree by degree.  Within each degree, it first computes
the syzygies of the presentation matrix, and then computes the second syzygies,
and so on.  This strategy uses Schreyer orders on the free modules in the
resolution which often improves efficiency.

Although similar to Strategy 2, this strategy does use Hilbert functions to aid
the computation.

See also
========

