sum(Complex) -- make the direct sum of all terms
************************************************

  * Function: *note sum: (Macaulay2Doc)sum,
  * Usage: 
        sum C
        sum f
  * Inputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, or f, a *note map of complexes:
        ComplexMap,
  * Outputs:
      * a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, or a *note matrix:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, if the input is a complex map

Description
===========

This is the forgetful functor from the category of chain complexes to the
category of modules. A chain complex $C$ is sent to the direct sum $\bigoplus_i
C_i$ of its terms. A map of chain complexes $f \colon C \to D$ is sent to the
direct sum $\bigoplus_i f_i \colon \bigoplus_i C_i \to \bigoplus_i D_i$.

