toChainComplex -- Converts a list of mutable matrices into a ChainComplex.
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        C = toChainComplex(M, F)
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of MutableMatrix type
      * F, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, the initial free module in
        the resolution. This is used to calculate the degrees in the maps.
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note complex: Complex,, 

Description
===========

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = ZZ/32003[vars(0..17)];                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : m1 = genericMatrix(R,a,3,3)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = | a d g |                                                               |
|     | b e h |                                                               |
|     | c f i |                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o2 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : m2 = genericMatrix(R,j,3,3)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = | j m p |                                                               |
|     | k n q |                                                               |
|     | l o r |                                                               |
|                                                                             |
|             3      3                                                        |
|o3 : Matrix R  <-- R                                                         |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : I = ideal(m1*m2-m2*m1)                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = ideal (d*k + g*l - b*m - c*p, b*j - a*k + e*k + h*l - b*n - c*q, c*j +  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     f*k - a*l + i*l - b*o - c*r, - d*j + a*m - e*m + d*n + g*o - f*p, - d*k |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     + b*m + h*o - f*q, - d*l + c*m + f*n - e*o + i*o - f*r, - g*j - h*m +   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     a*p - i*p + d*q + g*r, - g*k - h*n + b*p + e*q - i*q + h*r, - g*l - h*o |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     + c*p + f*q)                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o4 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : C = freeResolution I;                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : D = C[-10]                                                              |
|                                                                             |
|      1      8      33      60      61      32      5                        |
|o6 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R                         |
|                                                                             |
|     10     11     12      13      14      15      16                        |
|                                                                             |
|o6 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : MC = toMutableComplex D;                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : MC = first pruneComplex MC;                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i9 : D' = toChainComplex MC                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|      1      8      33      60      61      32      5                        |
|o9 = R  <-- R  <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R   <-- R                         |
|                                                                             |
|     0      1      2       3       4       5       6                         |
|                                                                             |
|o9 : Complex                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i10 : assert(betti D == betti D'[-10])                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Since the information about source of target of maps is not available, the
grading may be incorrect for general complexes.

See also
========

  * *note toMutableComplex: toMutableComplex, -- Converts a chain complex into
    a list of mutable matrices.

Ways to use toChainComplex:
===========================

  * "toChainComplex(List)"
  * "toChainComplex(List,Module)"

For the programmer
==================

